 can be shot. Columns 6–8 are where threats come from behind.\n\n**Layer 1: row-gated units.** Every row-gated unit gets weight +10 from each `player` cell of its row and a bias of −20. When the sub is in that row, the unit is linear in its content. In any other row it saturates at −1. Layer 2 sums each 8-unit family, adds 0.5·R0a and +7.5, and reads off the value of the sub's own row.\n\n- **Units 0–7, Z_s (fire/dodge, rows 1–8):**\n  - +1.5 per enemy in columns 0–4, which is a fire cue.\n  - −4.5 per enemy bullet in columns 2–4 (danger without reward), and −4 or −6 per danger in columns 6–8. These are dodge cues.\n  - Divers to the left or right count positive, which means \"stay here\".\n  - −1.2 per own bullet in columns 0–4, so the sub can leave once a shot is on its way.\n- **Units 8–15, V_s (vertical drive):** for rows within 4 of the sub's row, enemies and divers on the left (and divers on the right) pull the sub toward them. The pull falls with distance: 1.5, 0.9, 0.6, 0.45. There is also a small bias toward the middle rows.\n- **Units 16–23, Q_s (safety):** danger in columns 4–7 of the row above gives +6; the same in the row below gives −6.\n- **Unit 24, R0a:** the sub is in row 0.\n- **Unit 25, R0s:** the sub is in row 0 and row 1 is safe to enter.\n- **Unit 26, R1:** the sub is in row 1.\n- **Unit 27, SURF:** at least one diver (gauge cell (9,8) is lit) and oxygen below 60 (gauge cell (9,2) is dark).\n\n**Layer 2 decoders:**\n\n| Unit | Meaning |\n|---|---|\n| 0 FIRE | target in own row, fire |\n| 1 DODGE | threat in own row, leave the row |\n| 2 VDIR | signed vertical drive toward targets |\n| 3 SAFE_DN | row above is dangerous, don't go up |\n| 4 SAFE_UP | row below is dangerous, don't go down |\n| 5 SURF | surfacing needed |\n| 6 BAN | in row 1 with no surfacing need, so going up would mean surfacing without a diver |\n| 7, 8 | row-0 pass-throughs (R0s, R0a) |\n\n**Output logits:**\n- **Fire:** wins when there is a target and no threat.\n- **Dodge:** raises both up and down, and VDIR or the safety units pick the side.\n- **Otherwise:** the sub moves vertically toward targets.\n- **Surfacing:** forces up unless the row above is unsafe.\n- **Row 0:** the sub dives when row 1 is safe.\n\n```edits\nb3[1] = -30\nb3[3] = -30\nb1[0:24] = -20\nb1[8:12] = -19.85\nb1[12:16] = -20.15\nb1[8] = -19.5\nb1[15] = -20.5\nW1[60:120:6, 0] = 10\nW1[60:120:6, 8] = 10\nW1[60:120:6, 16] = 10\nW1[120:180:6, 1] = 10\nW1[120:180:6, 9] = 10\nW1[120:180:6, 17] = 10\nW1[180:240:6, 2] = 10\nW1[180:240:6, 10] = 10\nW1[180:240:6, 18] = 10\nW1[240:300:6, 3] = 10\nW1[240:300:6, 11] = 10\nW1[240:300:6, 19] = 10\nW1[300:360:6, 4] = 10\nW1[300:360:6, 12] = 10\nW1[300:360:6, 20] = 10\nW1[360:420:6, 5] = 10\nW1[360:420:6, 13] = 10\nW1[360:420:6, 21] = 10\nW1[420:480:6, 6] = 10\nW1[420:480:6, 14] = 10\nW1[420:480:6, 22] = 10\nW1[480:540:6, 7] = 10\nW1[480:540:6, 15] = 10\nW1[480:540:6, 23] = 10\n# Z units (fire/dodge) rows 1..8\nW1[61:120:6, 0] = [1.5,1.5,-4.5,-4.5,-4.5,0,-6,-6,-6,0]\nW1[62:120:6, 0] = [0,0,6,6,6,0,2,2,2,0]\nW1[63:90:6, 0] = -1.2\nW1[121:180:6, 1] = [1.5,1.5,-4.5,-4.5,-4.5,0,-6,-6,-6,0]\nW1[122:180:6, 1] = [0,0,6,6,6,0,2,2,2,0]\nW1[123:150:6, 1] = -1.2\nW1[181:240:6, 2] = [1.5,1.5,-4.5,-4.5,-4.5,0,-6,-6,-6,0]\nW1[182:240:6, 2] = [0,0,6,6,6,0,2,2,2,0]\nW1[183:210:6, 2] = -1.2\nW1[241:300:6, 3] = [1.5,1.5,-4.5,-4.5,-4.5,0,-6,-6,-6,0]\nW1[242:300:6, 3] = [0,0,6,6,6,0,2,2,2,0]\nW1[243:270:6, 3] = -1.2\nW1[301:360:6, 4] = [1.5,1.5,-4.5,-4.5,-4.5,0,-6,-6,-6,0]\nW1[302:360:6, 4] = [0,0,6,6,6,0,2,2,2,0]\nW1[303:330:6, 4] = -1.2\nW1[361:420:6, 5] = [1.5,1.5,-4.5,-4.5,-4.5,0,-6,-6,-6,0]\nW1[362:420:6, 5] = [0,0,6,6,6,0,2,2,2,0]\nW1[363:390:6, 5] = -1.2\nW1[421:480:6, 6] = [1.5,1.5,-4.5,-4.5,-4.5,0,-6,-6,-6,0]\nW1[422:480:6, 6] = [0,0,6,6,6,0,2,2,2,0]\nW1[423:450:6, 6] = -1.2\nW1[481:540:6, 7] = [1.5,1.5,-4.5,-4.5,-4.5,0,-6,-6,-6,0]\nW1[482:540:6, 7] = [0,0,6,6,6,0,2,2,2,0]\nW1[483:510:6, 7] = -1.2\n# Q units (safety of row above / below)\nW1[14